WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.377
Views are useful security-adjacent interfaces, but they should not be described as secure or compliant simply

00:00:06.377 --> 00:00:10.857
because they hide columns. Permissions still matter.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:16.137
Row-level security may matter. Application access paths matter.

00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:19.787
Compliance depends on a broader system of controls.

00:00:19.787 --> 00:00:23.537
Keep the claim proportional to what the view actually does.

00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:28.412
Views can reduce exposure by presenting only approved columns or rows,

00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:32.402
but they are not a complete security strategy by themselves.

00:00:32.402 --> 00:00:39.792
Understand ownership, privileges, and whether the view executes with invoker or definer-like behavior.

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:43.600
Sensitive data controls should be explicit and tested.
